<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.7.2: Finding Slope From Tables, Graphs, and Points</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00963</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.7.2: Finding Slope From Tables, Graphs, and Points</md:title>
    <md:uuid>069d1472-f34b-45d7-948a-ab63b5205107</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Recall that the <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">slope</term> of a line is the rate of change of the linear function. On the graph, it is the steepness of the line.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Activity</title>
        <exercise data-content-id="431b54f0-b83b-4912-bcc2-9bda8cb5d327" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> Find the slope of the line that connects \((0,0)\) and \((3,2)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(\frac23\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(\frac23\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="88ced5ad-5839-4508-b36d-779d23898f6a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> Find the slope of the line that connects \((4,2)\) and \((10,7)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(\frac56\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(\frac56\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="eef828ee-e5ce-4f27-8b8d-531aae6195c2" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> Find the slope of the line that connects \((1,-2)\) and \((2,5) \)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(7\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(7\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="3bf173be-910d-4ae4-a7c3-4d74aa5d1398" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> Find the slope of the line that connects \((-3,4)\) and \((-5,-2)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(3\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(3\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="dbdc4f2a-7893-4e9a-ba42-55e83f7eae6e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> Find the slope of the line that connects \((8, 3)\) and \((10, -9)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(-6\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(-6\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="84a05cf3-cfc6-4368-82c0-ce1a451b3371" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For numbers 6 – 9, use the graph to find the slope of the line that goes through the two points.</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_10_03_01.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
            </para>
            <para> A and B </para>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(-2\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(-2\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="081d3633-cb17-4803-8858-d3a8ca8c952b" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> A and D </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(2\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(2\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="41f98757-9a5a-4acf-84a9-ef139c4934c0" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> B and C </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(-1\) </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(-1\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="ca9ce444-7dfe-45ba-b8f3-17471cc14ebf" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> C and D </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(-8\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(-8\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="55714a1e-becd-4be8-8f38-b7000dd75e5e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> Determine the slope of the equation whose values are in the given table. </para>
            <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
              <thead>
        </thead>
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>1</entry>
                  <entry>3</entry>
                  <entry>5</entry>
                  <entry>7</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>\(y\)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>5</entry>
                  <entry>10</entry>
                  <entry>15</entry>
                  <entry>20</entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(\frac52\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(\frac52\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="6e60b31f-878d-44e9-ba3a-80f7683af806" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para> Determine the slope of the equation whose values are in the given table. Simplify your answer. </para>
            <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
              <thead>
        </thead>
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>2</entry>
                  <entry>5</entry>
                  <entry>8</entry>
                  <entry>11</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>\(y\)</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>4</entry>
                  <entry>1</entry>
                  <entry>-3</entry>
                  <entry>-6</entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(\frac{-3}{3}=-1\)</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(\frac{-3}{3}=-1\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
